### ConnectorSec security review — head `5f4a7d4`

**1. Cloud test password sent as Basic auth over plaintext HTTP** — [`client-v2/src/test/java/com/clickhouse/client/api/data_formats/JSONEachRowServerExceptionIT.java:178`](https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-java/blob/5f4a7d41d1aaaa5a9abdd561e8ac8a7e5b711ea5/client-v2/src/test/java/com/clickhouse/client/api/data_formats/JSONEachRowServerExceptionIT.java#L178)
- Scenario: `cloud.yml` (nightly on `main`, and on manual dispatch for a PR) runs `mvn --projects client-v2 verify` with `TEST_CLICKHOUSE_SECURE=true` and the shared Cloud test password in `TEST_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD`. Failsafe runs every `integration`-group class, this one included. In cloud mode `getServer(ClickHouseProtocol.HTTP)` resolves to the Cloud host on port 8443, but `httpBody()` always opens `http://`. The request, including the `Authorization: Basic …` header built at lines 180-182 from `ClickHouseServerForTest.getPassword()`, is written to the socket unencrypted before the TLS endpoint rejects it. That happens at least once for each of the four test invocations (2 tests × 2 parsers) on every cloud run, from a GitHub-hosted runner across the public internet. The rest of the suite uses TLS against Cloud (`setUp()` passes `isCloud()`; `cloud.yml`'s own `curl` calls use `https://…:8443`). The Bugbot thread on these lines covers the correctness side (cloud runs never get a real body); this is the credential side.
- Fix: build the URL with the scheme the suite already uses for Cloud (`BaseIntegrationTest.getConnectionProtocol()` returns `https` when `isCloud()`). Alternatively, skip the two raw-HTTP tests on Cloud with a `SkipException`, as `HttpTransportTests` does.
```diff
     private byte[] httpBody(String sql) throws Exception {
         ClickHouseNode node = getServer(ClickHouseProtocol.HTTP);
         HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) new URL(
-                "http://" + node.getHost() + ":" + node.getPort() + "/").openConnection();
+                getConnectionProtocol() + "://" + node.getHost() + ":" + node.getPort() + "/").openConnection();
         conn.setRequestMethod("POST");
```

<sub>Static review by ConnectorSec (ClickHouse Product Security); no PR code was executed.</sub>
